content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-107 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22950",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Current vibration: 5.5 mm/s RMS at the drive-end bearing housing falls in the manufacturer's Zone C range of 4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS, labelled “Restricted - plan maintenance.” It is 1.0 mm/s above the Zone B/C boundary at 4.5 and 1.6 mm/s below the Zone C/D boundary at 7.1. On the supplied reading it is not in the highest severity zone, so the immediate-stop rule is not triggered. This classification is provisional for the whole pump because the manual requires measurements on both housings and classification of the highest reading, but no current non-drive-end reading was reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Previous vibration: last month's 3.0 mm/s RMS falls in Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled “Long-term operation.” The reported increase is 2.5 mm/s RMS, and the classification has moved from Zone B to Zone C. Neither reading lies exactly on a zone boundary, so the figure's unstated boundary-assignment convention does not affect these classifications.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing temperature: 76 C is 6 C above the manufacturer's normal range, which extends up to 70 C, but remains 4 C below the 80 C alarm limit and 14 C below the 90 C trip limit. These limits apply to bearing-housing surface temperature. Because 76 C is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, the site rule requiring a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered; P2 is therefore assigned for planned investigation and maintenance rather than P1.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: no leakage was reported, so the troubleshooting table's shaft-seal leakage symptom is not present. The evidence provides no numerical allowable leak rate, and the report alone does not establish a need for mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Investigate shaft misalignment first: it is a documented probable cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, the two abnormal symptoms reported here.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate bearing wear next: it is also common to the manual's high-vibration and high-bearing-temperature cause lists. Bearing wear is a possibility to confirm by inspection, not a diagnosis established by the route readings alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check over-greasing: it is a documented cause of high bearing temperature, although it does not by itself explain the full vibration increase. Check the grease quantity before adding or removing grease.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect for impeller imbalance or damage, which the manual lists as a probable cause of high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate cavitation and check NPSH, the remaining documented high-vibration cause in the troubleshooting table. No NPSH or cavitation measurements are included in the report.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Plan the repair under Zone C's “Restricted - plan maintenance” classification. At job acceptance, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings in mm/s RMS, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, and verify the drive-end housing-surface temperature. If the highest vibration reading is in Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if bearing temperature exceeds 80 C, apply the site's priority-1 response.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump, check grease quantity and investigate operating evidence of cavitation/NPSH problems. Record the available alignment, temperature and vibration findings so that misalignment, over-greasing, cavitation and bearing/impeller defects can be distinguished rather than replacing parts solely on the route readings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any internal inspection or work on the seal, electrically isolate and lock out/tag out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, drain and vent the pump, and obtain the required line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If removal of the rotating assembly is required, use the HF-300 back pull-out arrangement, which permits removal without disturbing the casing or pipework. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so prepare the required lifting plan and use certified lifting equipment rather than manual lifting.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "With the assembly accessible, inspect both bearings and the impeller. Check for bearing wear or noise and for impeller imbalance or damage, and correlate these findings with the grease, alignment and NPSH checks. Do not conclude that the seal is defective merely from vibration and temperature when no leakage was reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apply the manual's bearing criterion: if either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair. If replacement is authorized, install drive-end bearing HF3-512 and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510 together; do not replace only the drive-end bearing. Use an approved detailed bearing-replacement procedure, which is not included in the supplied evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement is not part of the base scope. If inspection establishes that seal replacement is required, follow section 5.2's disassembly, sleeve-inspection, new-seal and new-casing-gasket requirements as modified by SB-2026-014: do not fit HF3-450; fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, for which no installation sleeve measurement is needed; inspect sleeve HF3-455 for scoring and replace it if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "During reassembly, replace casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing is opened. For disturbed fasteners covered by manual Table 5, tighten on lightly oiled threads to: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. The table's 25 Nm seal-gland value does not apply to an HF3-450B installation on this serial; use the bulletin's 30 Nm value instead.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment to a parallel offset tolerance of 0.05 mm and an angular tolerance of 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, restore the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry. After the work, repeat vibration measurements on both bearing housings and the housing-surface temperature check, classify the highest vibration result, and apply the same stop, alarm and trip criteria; a Zone D result requires reliability-engineer notification before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Conditional on the section 5.3 replacement criterion being met; supply with HF3-510 because bearings must be replaced as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Conditional on the section 5.3 replacement criterion being met; supply with HF3-512 as the matched pair-replacement scope.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Conditional: replace whenever the casing is opened, and include a new gasket if mechanical-seal replacement under section 5.2 is added.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal. Not required by the base inspection scope; use only if seal replacement is found necessary. It is the mandatory replacement for HF3-450 on this serial, needs no installation sleeve measurement, and has a 30 Nm seal-gland torque.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Conditional on applicable seal work revealing scoring deeper than 0.1 mm; otherwise reuse is not prohibited by the supplied bulletin.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of both suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the site's 25 kg lifting threshold. Obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment before lifting it.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Current reported vibration is Zone C, not the manufacturer's highest zone. If any subsequent highest-housing reading is classified Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current 76 C reading is below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip limits. If bearing temperature rises above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift; do not treat the present reading as having already met that site trigger.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If P-107 is confirmed to be on a chemically dosed line, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The specific sodium-hypochlorite dosing statement covers P-101 through P-106 on the filtered-water line and does not establish P-107's service, so chemical exposure must be confirmed before line break rather than assumed either way.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing work: Table 6 allows 6.0 hours with 2 technicians for replacement of the bearing pair. Apply this only if the pair-replacement criterion is confirmed; it is not an allowance for replacing only one bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional alignment work: allow 1.5 hours with 1 technician for laser alignment when alignment is performed, including after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional seal work: the manual's standard time for mechanical-seal replacement is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians if that scope is added. SB-2026-014 supplies no revised labour standard for HF3-450B, so no different time is inferred.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, while SB-2026-014 prohibits fitting HF3-450 and requires cartridge seal HF3-450B on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-107's serial HF3-22950 is within that range. Therefore, for any seal replacement under this work order, the bulletin issued 14 March 2026 governs and HF3-450B applies; the below-serial instruction to continue using HF3-450 does not apply to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: section 5.2 sends the technician to Table 5, which specifies 25 Nm for M10 seal-gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because this asset is serial HF3-22950 and therefore covered by the bulletin, use 30 Nm for the HF3-450B gland and do not use the manual's 25 Nm value. The bulletin does not supersede the other listed casing, impeller-nut or bearing-housing torques.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the current non-drive-end bearing-housing vibration reading? C06 requires readings on both housings and use of the highest; an unreported Zone D reading would change the stop decision and require reliability-engineer notification (C06, C07, C15).",
    "What operating restrictions, permitted run time, monitoring interval and repair completion date are intended by Zone C's “Restricted - plan maintenance” label? Figure 3 does not define them, and the supplied site procedure defines the P1 temperature trigger but not P2/P3 response times; the planner must set the due date (C07, C15).",
    "Was 76 C measured on the housing surface as required by the manual's temperature specification, and with what instrument? Confirm the measurement method before relying on the comparison with the 70/80/90 C limits (C01, C02).",
    "What are the actual grease quantity, alignment measurements, NPSH/cavitation data and bearing/impeller inspection findings? These will determine the corrective scope. No grease quantity/type specification or NPSH acceptance criterion is supplied in the evidence, so none should be invented (C09).",
    "Does the drive-end condition satisfy section 5.3's unqualified phrase “high temperature,” or is pair replacement to be based on wear/noise found during inspection? The evidence establishes that 76 C is above normal but below alarm, without explicitly mapping the phrase “high temperature” to one of those thresholds; obtain the responsible engineer's decision before automatic bearing condemnation (C02, C10).",
    "Is P-107 on chemically dosed service? C16 identifies only P-101 through P-106 on the filtered-water sodium-hypochlorite line; it does not identify P-107's fluid or line. Confirm this before line break to determine whether C15's chemical goggles and nitrile-glove control applies.",
    "Will inspection require opening the casing or disturbing the seal? This determines whether the casing gasket, seal, sleeve and conditional seal labour are needed. No leakage-based seal-replacement need is established by the report (C05, C09, C12).",
    "If bearing replacement is authorized, obtain the approved detailed disassembly, installation and lubrication procedure. The supplied manual excerpt states the pair-replacement rule and some reassembly torques but does not provide a complete bearing-replacement procedure (C10, C11).",
    "Table 6 supplies no standard labour allowance for troubleshooting, isolation/LOTO, lifting, internal inspection or post-work testing. These durations and any total job duration remain to be estimated by the planner rather than inferred from the bearing, seal or alignment standards (C12)."
  ]
}
